umentation Join Us --> Research Research Groups Observatories Key Laboratories Research Progress Research Programs Quick Links People Research Conferences Vacancies & Programs Location: Home > Research > Research Progress Research Progress • Researchers Report Dwarf Novae Unlikely to Be Type Ia Supernova Progenitors (2026-09-30) • Researchers Reveal Sharp Rise in Mass-Loss Rate Before a Rare Type Ia Superno... (2026-09-30) • Study Confirms Compact Companion around the RR Lyrae Star IY Lyr (2026-09-30) • Study Reports Gamma-Ray Excess Toward Radio-Quiet Narrow-Line Seyfert 1 Galax... (2026-09-28) • Research Advances Rapid Physical Inference for Type II Supernovae (2026-08-18) • Study Reveals Mi',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rp/',NULL,1,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','153fbfc5b16f62307069eaf6604b38739a2cf03ba7390bfa0e4253978477cbf9','3738bb0fa6ca2cca6bfa2d489d0b96b23309aa21c7a74d8568dda43ae1de238b',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://english.ynao.cas.cn/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
INSERT INTO documents(source_id,corpus,internal_id,topic,subtopic,exact_title,canonical_url,pdf_url,institution,author,country,geographic_area,organization_type,publication_date,updated_date,consulted_at,source_kind,language,factual_summary,essential_information,keywords,technology,performance,lock_concerned,maturity_trl,doi,official_identifier,licence,access_status,primary_secondary,peer_reviewed,quantitative_data,unit,evidence_location,contradiction,relevance_score,evidence_level,verification_level,http_status,control_comment,content_sha256,canonical_hash,official,public_access,free_access,active) SELECT id,'A','DOC-A9E0FA77C1B9055D52E0','research',NULL,'Researchers Report Dwarf Novae Unlikely to Be Type Ia Supernova Progenitors----Yunnan Observatories','https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rp/202609/t20260930_1201601.html',NULL,'*Yunnan Observatories',NULL,'China','Asia','official_research_institution',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-03T22:48:18.952Z','institutional_primary','en','Recently, PhD student LI Ruijie and Prof. WANG Bo from Yunnan Observatories, Chinese Academy of Sciences, reported new findings on dwarf novae. The team found that cyclic accretion in dwarf novae cannot sustain stable hydrogen burning on white dwarfs. Recurrent nova eruptions reduce the mass retention efficiency of white dwarfs, preventing them from growing to the Chandrasekhar mass limit through long-term accretion. Therefore, dwarf novae are unlikely to be progenitor systems of Type Ia supernovae. The study has been published in the international astronomical journal Astronomy & Astrophysics.','Recently, PhD student LI Ruijie and Prof. WANG Bo from Yunnan Observatories, Chinese Academy of Sciences, reported new findings on dwarf novae. The team found that cyclic accretion in dwarf novae cannot sustain stable hydrogen burning on white dwarfs. Recurrent nova eruptions reduce the mass retention efficiency of white dwarfs, preventing them from growing to the Chandrasekhar mass limit through long-term accretion. Therefore, dwarf novae are unlikely to be progenitor systems of Type Ia supernovae. The study has been published in the international astronomical journal Astronomy & Astrophysics.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rp/202609/t20260930_1201601.html',NULL,2,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','e8047570aee4be8f22399954c03d6f39f95d69f0c79538c880e05edb0613aace','a9e0fa77c1b9055d52e0b675d3328b6fae6996663510399eec37b61113ed883e',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://english.ynao.cas.cn/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
INSERT INTO documents(source_id,corpus,internal_id,topic,subtopic,exact_title,canonical_url,pdf_url,institution,author,country,geographic_area,organization_type,publication_date,updated_date,consulted_at,source_kind,language,factual_summary,essential_information,keywords,technology,performance,lock_concerned,maturity_trl,doi,official_identifier,licence,access_status,primary_secondary,peer_reviewed,quantitative_data,unit,evidence_location,contradiction,relevance_score,evidence_level,verification_level,http_status,control_comment,content_sha256,canonical_hash,official,public_access,free_access,active) SELECT id,'A','DOC-EE7054DC88F62AA2C7D0','research',NULL,'Solar Physics Group----Yunnan Observatories','https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rg/spg/',NULL,'*Yunnan Observatories',NULL,'China','Asia','official_research_institution',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-03T22:48:21.157Z','institutional_primary','en','Solar Physics is traditionally one of YNAO’s strongest fields of research. The Solar Physics group employs many experts in this field, and has access to immense amounts of resources in terms of instrumentation. Our academic mission is divided into 4 parts: project-oriented solar research, routine observations, database services, and the development of new technologies and instrumentation.','Solar Physics is traditionally one of YNAO’s strongest fields of research. The Solar Physics group employs many experts in this field, and has access to immense amounts of resources in terms of instrumentation. Our academic mission is divided into 4 parts: project-oriented solar research, routine observations, database services, and the development of new technologies and instrumentation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rg/spg/',NULL,1,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','ac86c085c2b38bccec9f360839fe3e1c4d775986f11025384c2cfbd8f30fb487','ee7054dc88f62aa2c7d0d1bbbd3a5b6e6d78bc5f26894270c0501bfc4237882b',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://english.ynao.cas.cn/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
INSERT INTO documents(source_id,corpus,internal_id,topic,subtopic,exact_title,canonical_url,pdf_url,institution,author,country,geographic_area,organization_type,publication_date,updated_date,consulted_at,source_kind,language,factual_summary,essential_information,keywords,technology,performance,lock_concerned,maturity_trl,doi,official_identifier,licence,access_status,primary_secondary,peer_reviewed,quantitative_data,unit,evidence_location,contradiction,relevance_score,evidence_level,verification_level,http_status,control_comment,content_sha256,canonical_hash,official,public_access,free_access,active) SELECT id,'A','DOC-D67F3B494B67885F651E','research',NULL,'Solar Site Survey and Coronal Observation Group----Yunnan Observatories','https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rg/ssscog/',NULL,'*Yunnan Observatories',NULL,'China','Asia','official_research_institution',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-03T22:48:21.126Z','institutional_primary','en','To advance the technique of ground-based observations and to solve the fundamental problems of solar physics, it is essential that optimum sites be allocated for the purpose of optical and IR solar observations in the near future. The western inland regions of China boast a homogeneous and stable atmosphere, an ample amount of sunlight hours, in addition to a high altitude. Such properties are ideal for solar observation, yet the region remains untouched by researchers in the field due to underdevelopment in the related areas. Therefore, prospecting for sites in these regions is a worthwhile activity for the development of solar research.','To advance the technique of ground-based observations and to solve the fundamental problems of solar physics, it is essential that optimum sites be allocated for the purpose of optical and IR solar observations in the near future. The western inland regions of China boast a homogeneous and stable atmosphere, an ample amount of sunlight hours, in addition to a high altitude. Such properties are ideal for solar observation, yet the region remains untouched by researchers in the field due to underdevelopment in the related areas. Therefore, prospecting for sites in these regions is a worthwhile activity for the development of solar research.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rg/ssscog/',NULL,1,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','7da40ce7acbc7da1f18b4ef8836d86515b1c4eac37717f071784c8a6d29764c0','d67f3b494b67885f651ea81ab5ece2090f45694b0ff9be1532de1d1495bda2a0',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://english.ynao.cas.cn/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
INSERT INTO documents(source_id,corpus,internal_id,topic,subtopic,exact_title,canonical_url,pdf_url,institution,author,country,geographic_area,organization_type,publication_date,updated_date,consulted_at,source_kind,language,factual_summary,essential_information,keywords,technology,performance,lock_concerned,maturity_trl,doi,official_identifier,licence,access_status,primary_secondary,peer_reviewed,quantitative_data,unit,evidence_location,contradiction,relevance_score,evidence_level,verification_level,http_status,control_comment,content_sha256,canonical_hash,official,public_access,free_access,active) SELECT id,'A','DOC-ADD2A891F7F41B6F47DC','research',NULL,'Stellar Astrophysics Group----Yunnan Observatories','https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rg/sag/',NULL,'*Yunnan Observatories',NULL,'China','Asia','official_research_institution',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-03T22:48:21.156Z','institutional_primary','en','The Stellar Astrophysics Group was created in the 1970s by Academician Runqian Huang. After over 30 years of development, the group has made significant breakthroughs in unconserved binary evolution theory, stellar wind shock theory, the effects of convective overshooting on stellar evolution, stellar evolution, formation of irregular objects, the period-luminosity relation of red supergiants, and the structure of the solar convective zone, among others.','The Stellar Astrophysics Group was created in the 1970s by Academician Runqian Huang. After over 30 years of development, the group has made significant breakthroughs in unconserved binary evolution theory, stellar wind shock theory, the effects of convective overshooting on stellar evolution, stellar evolution, formation of irregular objects, the period-luminosity relation of red supergiants, and the structure of the solar convective zone, among others.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rg/sag/',NULL,1,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','f8881cc74f61f6da8c9c113e008c804facb478a1fae07322b64c6d56c8419591','add2a891f7f41b6f47dc9bd02170c4de9e723b13c9e16142f5448301fd673e9b',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://english.ynao.cas.cn/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
INSERT INTO documents(source_id,corpus,internal_id,topic,subtopic,exact_title,canonical_url,pdf_url,institution,author,country,geographic_area,organization_type,publication_date,updated_date,consulted_at,source_kind,language,factual_summary,essential_information,keywords,technology,performance,lock_concerned,maturity_trl,doi,official_identifier,licence,access_status,primary_secondary,peer_reviewed,quantitative_data,unit,evidence_location,contradiction,relevance_score,evidence_level,verification_level,http_status,control_comment,content_sha256,canonical_hash,official,public_access,free_access,active) SELECT id,'A','DOC-7FBF2E036AECCACD03B5','research',NULL,'Study Confirms Compact Companion around the RR Lyrae Star IY Lyr----Yunnan Observatories','https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rp/202609/t20260930_1201606.html',NULL,'*Yunnan Observatories',NULL,'China','Asia','official_research_institution',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-03T22:48:19.782Z','institutional_primary','en','Researchers from the Yunnan Observatories (Chinese Academy of Sciences), working with the Ulugh Beg Astronomical Institute of Uzbekistan, have identified a compact companion orbiting the RR Lyrae star IY Lyr. By combining photometric, spectroscopic, and astrometric data—including LAMOST (Large Sky Area Multi-Object Fiber Spectroscopic Telescope) spectroscopy, ZTF (Zwicky Transient Facility), TESS (Transiting Exoplanet Survey Satellite), ASAS-SN (All-Sky Automated Survey for Supernovae), and dedicated BVRI observations from the Maidanak 60-cm telescope—they provided the first robust evidence for a companion with a mass of 1.37 solar masses around this RRc-type variable star.','Researchers from the Yunnan Observatories (Chinese Academy of Sciences), working with the Ulugh Beg Astronomical Institute of Uzbekistan, have identified a compact companion orbiting the RR Lyrae star IY Lyr. By combining photometric, spectroscopic, and astrometric data—including LAMOST (Large Sky Area Multi-Object Fiber Spectroscopic Telescope) spectroscopy, ZTF (Zwicky Transient Facility), TESS (Transiting Exoplanet Survey Satellite), ASAS-SN (All-Sky Automated Survey for Supernovae), and dedicated BVRI observations from the Maidanak 60-cm telescope—they provided the first robust evidence for a companion with a mass of 1.37 solar masses around this RRc-type variable star.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://english.ynao.cas.cn/research/rp/202609/t20260930_1201606.html',NULL,2,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','f98a30257527070b42bc4470ee1b1f52bc73a52d4bb7f27ea6ee7b717a9fd034','7fbf2e036aeccacd03b5dec8d68209d25690a63c545f09291a7337a3c666650d',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://english.ynao.cas.cn/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
